<title>HONG KONG: Arnhold 1996 net rises 19.15 percent.</title>
<headline>Arnhold 1996 net rises 19.15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   22.99     vs 19.30</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.42	vs 5.50</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  5.00 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    45.42     vs 38.12</p>
<p>    Turnover		     758.99    vs 626.36</p>
<p>    Company name		 Arnhold Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 23-30</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 9</p>
<p>NOTE - Arnhold Holdings is a building products and engineering company.</p>
<p>The expectional item represents a specific provision against a debtor who is in liquidation.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 9.17 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 2.75 cents) vs eight cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
